{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/pulls/66709","id":4779910402,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPc1QR88AAAABHOelAg","html_url":"https://github.com/github/gh-aw/pull/66709","diff_url":"https://github.com/github/gh-aw/pull/66709.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/github/gh-aw/pull/66709.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/issues/66709","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/pulls/66709/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/pulls/66709/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/issues/66709/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/statuses/f589401ee868290b1c1ddadb004da382e3551d33","number":66709,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[docs] Self-healing documentation fixes from issue analysis - 2026-10-07","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Self-Healing Documentation Fixes\n\nThis PR was automatically created by the Daily Documentation Healer workflow.\n\n### Gaps Fixed\n\n- Issue #65605: `[mcp-tools] Add governance/automations toolsets, fix stale schema enum` — removed the stale `search` and `experiments` entries from the \"Available\" GitHub toolsets list in `docs/src/content/docs/reference/github-tools.md`. Confirmed against the current source of truth (`pkg/workflow/data/github_toolsets_permissions.json`, v2.5): `experiments` was removed and its tools redistributed to `repos`/`orgs`/`users`/`issues`, and there is no `search` toolset entry anymore. Documenting either name as \"Available\" is actively wrong today — specifying `tools.github.toolsets: [search]` or `[experiments]` no longer maps to a real Go-side toolset.\n\nThe six additional toolsets named in #65605 (`code_quality`, `copilot`, `copilot_issue_intents`, `copilot_spaces`, `git`, `github_support_docs_search`) are **not** added to this page: they already exist in the permissions JSON, but `pkg/parser/schemas/main_workflow_schema.json`'s `github_toolset_name` enum (line ~14265) was never updated to include them, so a workflow author who writes `toolsets: [code_quality]` today hits a schema-validation error before the Go compiler ever sees it. Documenting them as \"Available\" would be misleading until that schema enum is fixed — that's a code change outside this docs-only PR's scope.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe underlying issue (#65605) was originally going to be fixed by PR #65615 (`[mcp-tools] Add governance and automations toolsets; sync schema enum`), which bundled the schema-enum sync together with two new, unconfirmed toolsets (`governance`, `automations`). That PR was closed **unmerged** after an automated code-quality review flagged real gaps (missing `github_tool_to_toolset` wiring for the new tools, and the `governance` toolset skipping GitHub App-only prerequisite enforcement) — a legitimate rejection, not an accidental closure. Issue #65605 itself was then auto-closed by expiry (`not_planned`) on 2026-10-06, so DDUw's \"closed as not_planned → cross-reference recent commits\" heuristic (`daily-doc-updater.md` Step 1c) never found a qualifying *merged* commit to treat as a documentation trigger — there wasn't one. The narrowly-scoped, uncontroversial part of the fix (removing the now-dead `search`/`experiments` names from the docs) was never re-attempted separately.\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 DDUw Improvement Suggestions</summary>\n\n### DDUw Improvement Suggestions\n\n1. **Fix broken guideline reference**: `daily-doc-updater.md` Step 3 instructs the agent to `cat .github/instructions/documentation.instructions.md`, but that file does not exist anywhere in the repository — the real guidelines live at `.github/skills/documentation/SKILL.md`. Update the path (two occurrences: Step 3's `cat` command and Step 5's \"Follow documentation guidelines from ...\" line) so DDUw actually loads real guidance instead of silently catting a missing file.\n2. **Add a direct reference-vs-data-file consistency check**: for reference pages that enumerate values sourced from a generated/data-driven list (e.g. `github-tools.md`'s toolset list vs. `pkg/workflow/data/github_toolsets_permissions.json`, or `artifacts.md` vs. `pkg/constants/*.go`), DDUw's Step 1c \"closed as not_planned\" path only cross-references *recent commits*. Add a lightweight \"data-file diff\" check that runs independent of whether a related commit landed: for known reference-pair files, directly diff the documented value list against the authoritative data/source file's current list, and flag drift even with zero qualifying commits in the 7-day window.\n3. **Track partially-rejected PRs for narrow re-extraction**: when a closed-unmerged PR bundles a safe, reviewer-uncontested change (e.g. \"sync the stale enum\") with a contested one (e.g. \"add two unconfirmed toolsets\"), DDUw currently has no mechanism to re-extract just the uncontested slice. Consider a heuristic: if a closed-unmerged PR's review comments single out *specific* files/sections as problematic, treat the untouched files/sections in that same diff as still-available fix material.\n\n</details>\n\n### Related Issues\n\n- Closes #65605\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code]((claude.com/redacted)\n\n\n<!-- gh-aw-tracker-id: daily-doc-healer -->\n\n> Generated by [📝 Daily Documentation Healer](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/actions/runs/37703947085) · claude · sonnet50 · 263.6 AIC · ⌖ 35.6 AIC · ⊞ 6.6K · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agithub%2Fgh-aw+%22gh-aw-workflow-id%3A+daily-doc-healer%22&type=pullrequests)\n> - [x] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-10-10T23:56:29.316Z --> on Oct 10, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC-08:00\n\n<!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Daily Documentation Healer, gh-aw-tracker-id: daily-doc-healer, engine: claude, model: claude-sonnet-5, id: 37703947085, workflow_id: daily-doc-healer, run: https://github.com/github/gh-aw/actions/runs/37703947085 -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-expires-type: pull-request -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: daily-doc-healer -->\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: github/gh-aw/daily-doc-healer -->","labels":[{"id":9099894122,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPc1QR88AAAACHmVdag","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","description":"Improvements or additions to documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9139391526,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPc1QR88AAAACIMAMJg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/labels/automation","name":"automation","description":null,"color":"ededed","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-07T23:56:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T19:07:29Z","closed_at":"2026-10-08T00:42:57Z","merged_at":"2026-10-08T00:42:57Z","merge_commit_sha":"251d3491a234826851e0a0134516c05c93212760","assignee":nu